speechtext:
It reads as follows:
Whereas a considerable portion of the population of Newfoundland has for generations been compelled by economic necessity to rely largely upon certain species of sea birds, described as migratory non-game birds in the migratory birds treaty, for their subsistence during certain seasons of the year;
And whereas immediate strict application of the migratory birds regulations, as they apply to other provinces, within Newfoundland would cause serious hardship to the above residents of that province;
Therefore be it resolved that this conference recommends that in extending the provisions of the Migratory Birds Convention Act and regulations to Newfoundland, sympathetic consideration be given to the situation of the Newfoundland residents above mentioned; and that, within the obligations imposed by the migratory birds treaty, the greatest possible patience and leniency should be exercised in enforcing the regulations in that province during the period considered necessary for adjustment.
There is a note that it was carried unanimously. I do not want to put anything on Hansard that is objectionable. I was merely trying to save some time here.
